        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "61fb2467-0dd9-563c-8874-41b358310cc5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Caldera de Taburiente National Park, Teide National Park, La Palma, Tenerife, Canary Islands, Spain\n- Products: Echium wildpretii subsp. trichosiphon, Adenocarpus viscosus\n- Topics: geological features, plant distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Caldera de Taburiente National Park is a large geological feature on the island of La Palma in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Teide National Park is a national park located on Tenerife in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on La Palma in Caldera de Tabouriente.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus can be found above 1800 meters on Tenerife, where it is a dominant shrub in Teide National Park.\n- Adenocarpus viscosus also occurs in parts of Corona Forestal Nature Park and Reserva Especial de las Palomas on Tenerife.\n- The chunk mentions Echium wildpretii subsp. trichosiphon, but provides no complete fact about it.",
